          "date": "2026-10-21 17:57:14.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20996 mgs: return count from ir_timeout_store()",
        "message": "LU-20996 mgs: return count from ir_timeout_store()\n\nir_timeout_store() returns the result of kstrtou64(), which is\n0 on success. A sysfs store function must return the number of\nbytes that it used. Thus a write to mgs.MGS.ir_timeout sets the\nvalue, but lctl set_param reports \"wrote only 0\" and EINVAL.\nThe procfs handler had the same defect before the sysfs move.\n\nReturn count when the parse succeeds.\n\nir_timeout is a time64_t, but kstrtou64() takes a u64 pointer.\nA value above S64_MAX thus becomes a negative timeout. Parse\nthe value with kstrtos64() and reject a negative value.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 860e20e42ddc (\"LU-9325 obd: replace lprocfs_str_to_s64\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5\nChange-Id: I7cd5c15dad7d3f68c454b69c194678e14ed12235\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
